Subject: [PATCH] Expose persist first inventory checkpoints


diff --git a/src/main/java/org/bukkit/entity/Player.java b/src/main/java/org/bukkit/entity/Player.java
index dab57c9b8938b0fe88e8af77d30ee184de78b1c8..afafcf3fbebb48a735da1057289cb04cb0f08e46 100644
--- a/src/main/java/org/bukkit/entity/Player.java
+++ b/src/main/java/org/bukkit/entity/Player.java
@@ -561,6 +561,32 @@ public interface Player extends HumanEntity, Conversable, OfflinePlayer, PluginM
         return CompletableFuture.failedFuture(new UnsupportedOperationException("Asynchronous player saves are not supported"));
     }
 
+    /**
+     * Persists proposed storage contents and persistent data before applying them to this session.
+     * The editor receives an isolated container on the player owner. Other data is captured normally.
+     * Until completion, lifecycle saves include this proposal while its original inventory remains
+     * unchanged. The live storage and edited keys are applied only after a flushed checkpoint and
+     * a final owner check. Health, combat and world state are not suspended.
+     * Login reads wait for the final decision. A synchronous reload during the operation reads
+     * actual captured state, without the proposed inventory or persistent data edits.
+     *
+     * <p>If the inventory changes, the player dies, or {@code canApply} declines, actual player data
+     * is saved before completing with {@code false}. A retired session or storage failure completes
+     * exceptionally; an accepted proposal may already be on disk and must be reconciled using the
+     * caller's persistent marker. Cancelling the returned future does not cancel accepted work.</p>
+     *
+     * @param storageContents exactly 36 storage slots, copied on acceptance; null slots are empty
+     * @param editPersistentData edits to the saved container, without changing the live container
+     * @param canApply final permission check on the player owner; it must not perform IO
+     * @return true when applied, false after a durable rejection, or an exceptional unknown outcome
+     */
+    default CompletableFuture<Boolean> applyInventoryCheckpointAsync(
+            @Nullable ItemStack[] storageContents,
+            java.util.function.Consumer<org.bukkit.persistence.PersistentDataContainer> editPersistentData,
+            java.util.function.BooleanSupplier canApply) {
+        return CompletableFuture.failedFuture(new UnsupportedOperationException("Inventory checkpoints are not supported"));
+    }
+
